Title: 200 AMSTERDAM: THE VERTICAL CITY
Credit: Written for the Screen by
Author: Danny Bouldiez
Episode: PART 13: THIRTY DAYS EARLY & THE STORY OF THE SPARROWS (CHAPTER 12)

====

EXT. HUDSON RIVER ESPLANADE - DAWN

The storm has passed. A pale, golden dawn breaks over the Manhattan skyline.

200 Amsterdam stands dark and empty against the morning light—scarred, tilted, but still standing.

A line of emergency rescue tents lines the esplanade. 

JULIAN and his MOTHER sit together on a wooden bench, wrapped in wool blankets, watching the sunrise over the river.

ARIS THORNE and DEVS ONE stand by the water's edge, looking up at the tower.

High on the iron lattice of the lower scaffolding, a small brown SPARROW lands. 

Then another. Then a dozen.

They begin to sing—their chirps clean, sharp, and resilient in the morning air.

                         DEVS ONE
          They came back.

                         ARIS
          (smiling softly)
          The sparrows always come back. They know the rock never dies. 
          It just waits for us to learn how to live upon it.

SUPER: "The ground remembers. Love is the only force capable of holding everyone together when the wheel of fortune spins out of control."

FADE OUT.

TITLE CARD:
